rement describes;\ncase-insensitive search is the C-BetterSearch extension.\n","tags":["Level-9"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":107,"deletions":1},"md":{"insertions":1,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"37ad0d70ed1cbda5397b1a2748c7b8fc17658112","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge JavaDoc into master","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"5e899e79112465a4149855c37b3ab5008a83040e","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge CodingStandard into master","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"27c5d0a8dc506965a4ff92dd19298527f0dbf0e2","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge L9 into master","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-09-01T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"2e50ef27deca8c8c16e3293424a5e57bcb0fc99e","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"A-CheckStyle: Add Checkstyle to the Gradle build","messageBody":"Add the se-edu Checkstyle config under config/checkstyle and apply the\ncheckstyle plugin, so gradlew build now fails on style violations.\n\nFix the 18 violations it reported:\n\n- indent the arrow switch cases in Crack and Storage\n- give the command switch in Crack an explicit default branch\n","tags":["A-CheckStyle"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"gradle":{"insertions":5,"deletions":0},"java":{"insertions":19,"deletions":17}}},{"hash":"f2621724744aa0a85439541674b9d021150d67ee","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Level-10: Add a JavaFX GUI","messageBody":"Add a chat window built with JavaFX, following the JavaFX tutorial:\nLauncher starts Main, Main loads MainWindow.fxml, and every message is a\nDialogBox. Point mainClass at the launcher so gradlew run opens it.\n\nThe window reuses the command handling instead of repeating it. Ui now\nsends every line through a print hook, so GuiUi can collect the same\nwording for a bubble rather than printing it, and Crack accepts the\ninterface it should talk through.\n\nThe text UI still runs via crack.Crack, which keeps the JUnit tests on\nthe same code path the window uses.\n","tags":["Level-10"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"gradle":{"insertions":15,"deletions":1},"fxml":{"insertions":26,"deletions":0},"java":{"insertions":265,"deletions":33}}},{"hash":"a4c66d3c3fbbf4e375fa7f7dd30e5ad9301e4ae0","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"A-Varargs: Take several tasks in TaskList.add","messageBody":"TaskList.add now takes varargs, so a caller with a handful of tasks can\nhand them over in one call. Callers passing a single task, such as Crack,\nare unchanged.\n\nCollapse the runs of add calls in TaskListTest and StorageTest, which is\nwhere building a list several tasks at a time actually happens.\n","tags":["A-Varargs"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":18,"deletions":17}}},{"hash":"6bdf95a451930ff8db30f303d17fb8f85bb89d71","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"resolve checkstyle issues","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"b845a387d195e59edca184c709a0a1ce08d0c08c","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"add JavaFX gui","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"73463757fcdff20d9a246e89eb5cbba9ea04bfa4","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"add varargs support","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]}]},"authorFileTypeContributionMap":{"Alexc09":{"java":1662,"md":35,"fxml":26,"sh":0,"bat":0,"gradle":21,"txt":16}},"authorContributionVariance":{"Alexc09":62539.062},"authorDisplayNameMap":{"Alexc09":"CS2103-F12-1 ALEX.. HAO"}}
